<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 2 May, from 1519 to 1972.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1519</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Leonardo da Vinci dies at Amboise</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Leonardo died at Clos Lucé, the manor near Amboise given to him by Francis I. Painter of the Mona Lisa and The Last Supper, he also left thousands of pages of notes on anatomy, engineering and nature.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1536</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Anne Boleyn is arrested and taken to the Tower</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Queen Anne Boleyn was arrested at Greenwich on charges of adultery, incest and treason. She was beheaded at the Tower seventeen days later, and Henry VIII married Jane Seymour within days.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1670</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles II charters the Hudson's Bay Company</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The company received a monopoly of trade across the lands draining into Hudson Bay, a vast territory named Rupert's Land. It remains one of the oldest commercial enterprises in the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-bay">Hudson Bay</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1808</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Madrid rises against French occupation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Crowds in Madrid attacked French troops in the Dos de Mayo uprising, which was suppressed with mass executions painted by Goya. Revolt spread across Spain and began the Peninsular War.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peninsular-war">Peninsular War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1863</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stonewall Jackson is shot by his own men at Chancellorsville</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Returning from a night reconnaissance, General Thomas 'Stonewall' Jackson was hit by fire from Confederate pickets. He died of pneumonia eight days later, a grave loss to Lee.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1945</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Berlin garrison surrenders to the Red Army</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General Helmuth Weidling surrendered the German forces in Berlin to the Soviets two days after Hitler's suicide. Germany's unconditional surrender followed within a week.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1972</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">J. Edgar Hoover dies after 48 years leading the FBI</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">J. Edgar Hoover died in Washington, having led the Bureau and its predecessor since 1924. He built a modern federal police force but also used it to spy on activists and politicians.</p></li></ol>
